1
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:09,020
YAMU, YAMU, YAMU, YAMU, YAMU!

2
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:31,498
You're on the move!

3
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:05,080
Comfy, are we?

4
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:09,940
Release me at once.

5
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:14,984
From where I'm standing, it looks like
you're in no position to be making demands.

6
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:17,620
You won't get away with this.

7
00:01:18,340 --> 00:01:19,170
Wrong.

8
00:01:19,253 --> 00:01:21,437
I've already destroyed
one of your cohorts,

9
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:24,049
and I have the Millennium
Ring to prove it.

10
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:25,920
Then it's true.

11
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:28,357
It's painful, isn't it, old man?

12
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:30,720
To lose someone you care about?

13
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:33,220
Well, try losing your whole village!

14
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:36,520
Please, if you'll just let me explain.

15
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:42,280
You destroyed my homeland, took away
my family, and left me with nothing!

16
00:01:43,340 --> 00:01:47,420
Now it's time to pay
the price by serving me.

17
00:01:48,860 --> 00:01:50,897
I know that you have a dark side.

18
00:01:50,980 --> 00:01:52,940
It just needs to be brought out.

19
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:55,800
And I'm just the man to do it!

20
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:03,560
My Millennium Puzzle is
sensing a dark presence.

21
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:06,050
Tharo!

22
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:07,260
What is it?

23
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:12,640
A village along the Nile was
attacked a few moments ago. What?

24
00:02:13,260 --> 00:02:15,520
Look, one of our sanctuaries.

25
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:18,140
But whose are Gnardins?

26
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:26,100
There's only one person capable
of an act of treason like this.

27
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:27,830
Bakura.

28
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:33,900
We mustn't let him get away, then!

29
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,647
Surround the palace at once!

30
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:38,617
Let no stone in the courtyard go unturned!

31
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:39,935
He could be anywhere!

32
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:49,270
He...

33
00:02:49,353 --> 00:02:50,520
must be... stopped!

34
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:52,628
What happened here, Master?

35
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,500
Speak to me!

36
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:56,080
Who did this?

37
00:02:57,060 --> 00:02:58,180
Pure evil.

38
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,360
Are you all right?

39
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:04,000
Yes, he's going to be fine.

40
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:06,654
He's just been under incredible strain.

41
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:11,314
We cannot let that rogue continue to
get away with these despicable acts.

42
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:14,820
Let us take him down once and for all.

43
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:16,000
He shall pay.

44
00:03:17,380 --> 00:03:19,320
He's taken the captain's horse.

45
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:20,980
Don't let him escape.

46
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:24,777
Halt in the name of the pharaoh.

47
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:27,020
I'm warning you!

48
00:03:31,140 --> 00:03:33,600
Interfere and face the wrath of Diabo!

49
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:41,760
Soon the mighty pharaoh has taken my fate!

50
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:46,760
This madness ends here!

51
00:03:47,020 --> 00:03:48,860
Gods of Egypt, hear me!

52
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:55,430
Behold!

53
00:03:55,513 --> 00:03:57,520
Slifer the Sky Dragon!

54
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:02,780
Well, it seems we have
an unexpected guest!

55
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:09,540
The ultimate battle for the future
of mankind shall begin once again!

56
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:12,400
Only this time, I shall prevail!

57
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:14,350
Bakura!

58
00:04:14,433 --> 00:04:17,551
Stop running like a coward and
face up to what you've done!

59
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:32,600
It's the pharaoh!

60
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:36,800
And that is a big red dragon!

61
00:04:37,260 --> 00:04:41,160
This sort of thing used to
surprise me, but now, not so much.

62
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:44,302
Did anyone get a good look
at who he was chasing?

63
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:45,470
The car!

64
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:48,040
Come on, guys! We gotta help!

65
00:05:00,580 --> 00:05:03,377
I know all of your secrets are none.

66
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:05,820
I know what you did at Kal Elna.

67
00:05:06,020 --> 00:05:09,640
These events may have
occurred 15 long years ago,

68
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:13,340
but time doesn't heal all wounds.

69
00:05:17,820 --> 00:05:20,477
My pharaoh, we've lost our
stronghold to the north,

70
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:23,677
and the enemy continues their
march towards the capital.

71
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:27,477
With our remaining armies, how
long can we withstand their attack?

72
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:30,160
If all goes well, perhaps a week.

73
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:33,320
So the end has come.

74
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:37,320
With all due respect, giving
up is not an option, sir.

75
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:40,977
This conflict will not just
decide the fate of our country,

76
00:05:41,060 --> 00:05:42,477
but that of the entire world.

77
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:45,740
If we were to allow the enemy
to advance much further,

78
00:05:46,020 --> 00:05:48,491
they would seize our Millennium Spellbook.

79
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:50,520
They must not succeed.

80
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:55,017
It is said that whomever deciphers
the book's ancient text will be

81
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:59,200
able to control a power known only
by the Egyptian gods themselves.

82
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:04,260
Yes, and perhaps we can tap
that power to defeat the enemy.

83
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:06,993
We've been through this before, Aknaden.

84
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:09,997
No one has been able
to decode those spells.

85
00:06:10,080 --> 00:06:11,840
That's not true, sir.

86
00:06:12,260 --> 00:06:13,848
We have had a breakthrough.

87
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:15,130
What?

88
00:06:15,213 --> 00:06:17,668
Are you saying that
you've decoded the book?

89
00:06:17,940 --> 00:06:22,280
Not quite, but I have managed
to decipher one of its spells.

90
00:06:22,740 --> 00:06:28,420
It's a ritual of sorts, allowing the
spellcaster to forge seven mystical treasures.

91
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:31,857
These Millennium Items could eliminate the

92
00:06:31,940 --> 00:06:34,940
invaders and bring tranquility
to Egypt once again.

93
00:06:35,320 --> 00:06:38,060
And just how long will
it take to create them?

94
00:06:38,980 --> 00:06:43,200
According to the spell, the task
will take seven days. Fortunately,

95
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:45,597
I've already begun experimenting with the

96
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:48,386
shadow magic necessary
to fashion these items.

97
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:52,340
If it will bring peace, fine.

98
00:06:54,060 --> 00:06:54,890
Proceed.

99
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:59,998
Go forth and create these seven
millennium items in the name of Egypt.

100
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:03,357
The fate of this kingdom
rests with you, my brother.

101
00:07:03,440 --> 00:07:04,734
Make our father proud.

102
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:08,480
In order to save our kingdom,

103
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:11,817
I must do the unthinkable, and
if my actions are discovered,

104
00:07:11,900 --> 00:07:13,312
people may seek revenge.

105
00:07:14,060 --> 00:07:18,040
So, for your own protection, no
one must ever know I have a family.

106
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:21,160
You must run as far from here as you can.

107
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:23,100
It's for your own good.

108
00:07:23,380 --> 00:07:26,020
I wish there was another solution to this.

109
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:27,340
So do I.

110
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,440
And please remember,

111
00:07:29,680 --> 00:07:34,621
it is essential that Seto never learn the
truth about who I am, as long as he lives.

112
00:07:35,620 --> 00:07:36,880
I'm nodding!

113
00:07:37,880 --> 00:07:41,660
Farewell, my love, and my dear son, Sidhu.

114
00:07:48,140 --> 00:07:51,060
I've called you here today for one reason.

115
00:07:51,360 --> 00:07:53,677
You are the Pharaoh's strongest soldiers,

116
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:56,525
and the very future of
our land depends on you.

117
00:07:56,660 --> 00:07:58,180
Now listen closely.

118
00:07:58,640 --> 00:08:01,060
You must never repeat what I say.

119
00:08:01,300 --> 00:08:03,980
And now I shall make sure of that.

120
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:10,560
Let my voice penetrate your very core!

121
00:08:12,220 --> 00:08:14,660
Yes, master, are none.

122
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:18,700
Gentlemen, my voice is
the voice of reason,

123
00:08:19,100 --> 00:08:22,840
the voice of peace, the
only voice you will obey.

124
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:26,137
You have been handpicked to take part in a

125
00:08:26,220 --> 00:08:29,320
ritualistic experiment to
save the land of Egypt.

126
00:08:30,240 --> 00:08:32,497
There is no turning back now.

127
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:37,168
Our mission begins tonight in a small
village on the outskirts of our kingdom.

128
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:39,120
To Kal Elna!

129
00:08:39,440 --> 00:08:40,800
To Kal Elna!

130
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:51,000
The Pharaoh must never learn of the
events that are about to follow.

131
00:08:51,360 --> 00:08:53,260
According to the Book of Spells,

132
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:57,911
evil spirits must be captured in order
to create the Seven Millennium Items.

133
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,660
Of this, my brother would never approve.

134
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:12,040
We stand before the evil
village of Kal-El-Na.

135
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:16,660
The inhabitants are possessed with
the darkest spirits known to man.

136
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:21,997
That's why they have been raiding our royal
tombs and stealing our riches for years.

137
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:25,080
But tonight we shall put
an end to their evil ways.

138
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:27,860
Capture those spirits, men! Yeah!

139
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:30,420
Our spirits are lies!

140
00:09:32,180 --> 00:09:34,140
Relinquish your evil spirits!

141
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:36,700
Leave our village at once!

142
00:09:36,960 --> 00:09:38,120
This is an outrage!

143
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:39,870
Die!

144
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:48,640
It's time to put your souls to good use!

145
00:09:50,780 --> 00:09:53,900
Spirits of darkness, I command thee!

146
00:09:56,020 --> 00:10:01,700
Offer up your power, your very essence,
so that the Millennium Items may be born!

147
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:08,220
It is not from gold that
these treasures are forged,

148
00:10:08,400 --> 00:10:11,753
but from the darkness that
lies within the hearts of men.

149
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:22,200
It worked! Behold!

150
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:23,920
The Millennium Items!

151
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:27,080
What's going on?

152
00:10:35,580 --> 00:10:37,100
Master Akkadon!

153
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:39,144
Perhaps we've angered the gods!

154
00:10:42,460 --> 00:10:47,100
It looks as if the seven
items fit inside that stone!

155
00:10:54,100 --> 00:10:56,240
What have I unleashed?

156
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:18,400
What do you want from me?

157
00:11:18,660 --> 00:11:22,400
Return those treasures
to their resting place.

158
00:11:23,020 --> 00:11:25,380
These items belong to us.

159
00:11:29,220 --> 00:11:32,880
Shadow creature, unhack me at once.

160
00:11:36,440 --> 00:11:39,320
Master Ahnodden, we must leave now.

161
00:11:41,500 --> 00:11:42,600
Not without this!

162
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:46,360
It's gone!

163
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:03,360
I made it.

164
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:05,180
I'm home.

165
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:13,080
It seems the king of Egypt has given up.

166
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:15,740
Those fools!

167
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:17,620
They all ran away!

168
00:12:18,180 --> 00:12:21,420
Men, those cowards have
abandoned their kingdom,

169
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:24,580
which means that Egypt belongs to us now!

170
00:12:36,880 --> 00:12:38,900
Look at these poor fools!

171
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:41,400
They face us with an army of seven!

172
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:43,800
Show no mercy, men!

173
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:50,180
In the name of Egypt,
Millennium Items activate now!

174
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:55,760
Mighty spirits, protect our kingdom!

175
00:13:12,820 --> 00:13:15,140
I shall never forget that day.

176
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:19,560
It was both my greatest
achievement and my darkest hour.

177
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:25,900
My efforts had saved Egypt from destruction,
but I deserted my family to do so.

178
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:30,200
And my only son, Seto, would
never know of his noble ancestry.

179
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:34,680
On behalf of King Aknam Cannon,

180
00:13:34,880 --> 00:13:38,821
let us welcome the new guardian of
the Millennium Rod, Master Seto.

181
00:13:39,260 --> 00:13:42,077
Though raised by peasants,
he has risen to excellence,

182
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:45,600
passing his tests with the
highest scores we've ever seen.

183
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:48,280
Welcome to my sacred court.

184
00:13:49,860 --> 00:13:52,331
Many thanks for this great honor, my king.

185
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:53,880
I'll serve thee well.

186
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:57,000
From this day forth, I
am your humble servant.

187
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:02,294
As the youngest royal guardian, you
will sit at the right hand of my son,

188
00:14:02,540 --> 00:14:03,481
the future king.

189
00:14:03,860 --> 00:14:05,331
Thank you, your highness.

190
00:14:07,140 --> 00:14:09,597
You've been unusually quiet, Aknaden.

191
00:14:09,680 --> 00:14:10,740
Are you all right?

192
00:14:11,040 --> 00:14:12,280
I was in shock.

193
00:14:12,580 --> 00:14:14,639
There, kneeling before the pharaoh,

194
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:18,060
unbeknownst to anyone in
the room, was my own son.

195
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:21,597
The boy I abandoned and
stripped of his royal heritage

196
00:14:21,680 --> 00:14:25,197
had now overcome every obstacle
and risen to greatness,

197
00:14:25,280 --> 00:14:27,100
All on his own merit.

198
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:31,620
At that moment, I realized it
is you who should be Pharaoh.

199
00:14:32,420 --> 00:14:34,760
My son deserves to be king.

200
00:14:35,100 --> 00:14:36,960
And mark my words.

201
00:14:37,180 --> 00:14:38,720
King he shall become!

202
00:14:46,140 --> 00:14:47,620
All right, do you mind?

203
00:14:48,100 --> 00:14:51,512
I think it's about time we
showed off your newest ability!

204
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:53,694
Illusionary Shockwave!

205
00:14:59,520 --> 00:15:03,020
Dearbound steals the abilities
of the enemies it defeats.

206
00:15:03,440 --> 00:15:06,300
That last attack came courtesy of Mahan.

207
00:15:06,600 --> 00:15:07,660
That can't be.

208
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:11,300
Sliver, lightning, blast.

209
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:14,070
Yes.

210
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:21,580
Sorry, Farrow, but you're
not in the clear just yet.

211
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:25,250
Now!

212
00:15:32,660 --> 00:15:33,490
No!

213
00:15:33,573 --> 00:15:35,180
You pay for that!

214
00:15:35,600 --> 00:15:38,100
You've forgotten who you're dealing with!

215
00:15:38,380 --> 00:15:40,997
And you seem to have
forgotten that this battle

216
00:15:41,080 --> 00:15:43,257
isn't one of your little card tournaments,

217
00:15:43,340 --> 00:15:44,170
Sparrow!

218
00:15:44,253 --> 00:15:48,640
And as you're about to find out,
in this arena I have the advantage!

219
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:51,420
Diomalt, destroy the city!

220
00:15:53,400 --> 00:15:54,230
Look!

221
00:15:54,380 --> 00:15:55,220
In the sky!

222
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:57,640
What is that thing? One thing!

223
00:15:57,900 --> 00:15:59,194
There's nothing there!

224
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:00,880
Oh no!

225
00:16:02,860 --> 00:16:05,060
Make way for his majesty!

226
00:16:08,360 --> 00:16:09,190
Stop!

227
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:11,560
This fight is between you and me!

228
00:16:12,540 --> 00:16:13,370
Very well!

229
00:16:13,453 --> 00:16:14,771
Then it's time to decide!

230
00:16:15,420 --> 00:16:18,360
Continue to fight me or save your people!

231
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:29,720
I think that red monster just saved us!

232
00:16:31,620 --> 00:16:32,640
Quick, run!

233
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:35,500
Slifer, protect these villagers!

234
00:16:36,620 --> 00:16:40,860
How noble of you to use your monster
as a shield to save these fools!

235
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:43,720
But how much abuse can Slifer endure?

236
00:16:44,360 --> 00:16:45,720
I guess we'll see!

237
00:16:53,460 --> 00:16:55,360
Looks like a dead end, pharaoh.

238
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:59,335
So much for rescuing those
precious villagers of yours.

239
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:03,696
No harm shall befall the
people of my kingdom, Bakura.

240
00:17:03,880 --> 00:17:04,900
Mark my words.

241
00:17:05,360 --> 00:17:06,680
Sniper, attack!

242
00:17:10,040 --> 00:17:13,160
Whoa, those are definitely not holograms.

243
00:17:14,100 --> 00:17:15,080
Uh, no.

244
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:20,830
What?!

245
00:17:20,913 --> 00:17:23,760
I refuse to let you put this
city in any more danger!

246
00:17:24,260 --> 00:17:26,980
Sliver, take this fight to the skies!

247
00:17:29,780 --> 00:17:32,280
My people are safe from your attacks!

248
00:17:32,660 --> 00:17:35,160
Your Egyptian god may control the skies!

249
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:36,510
However,

250
00:17:36,593 --> 00:17:38,377
my Diabaunt commands the darkness,

251
00:17:38,460 --> 00:17:41,578
making him infinitely more
powerful than your dragon!

252
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:44,580
It's gone!

253
00:17:45,020 --> 00:17:46,237
What have you done?!

254
00:17:46,320 --> 00:17:50,780
My creature has the ability to move
in shadow, completely undetectable.

255
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:54,980
And by the time it reveals
itself, it shall be too late.

256
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:03,740
Your bond with the gods is so strong
that when they feel pain, so do you.

257
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:07,560
Now, how shall I conclude
this battle of ours, Pharaoh?

258
00:18:08,060 --> 00:18:10,648
Shall I destroy your
Slytherin or this city?

259
00:18:11,380 --> 00:18:13,977
Or perhaps I'll have Dearbound crush you.

260
00:18:14,060 --> 00:18:18,942
Of course, there is a simpler way to spare
yourself and your city from destruction.

261
00:18:19,140 --> 00:18:21,800
Just surrender your
Millennium Puzzle to me.

262
00:18:22,220 --> 00:18:26,260
If you do, I promise to leave you
and your precious villagers alone.

263
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:30,857
If I hand over the Millennium Puzzle,
Makuro will become unstoppable.

264
00:18:30,940 --> 00:18:32,999
But I can't let him harm my people.

265
00:18:35,440 --> 00:18:37,740
A wise decision, your highness.

266
00:18:39,040 --> 00:18:40,497
This just might work.

267
00:18:40,580 --> 00:18:44,620
If I can distract him for long
enough, I may be able to defeat him.

268
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:46,200
It's my only hope.

269
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:50,300
Now, get off your high
horse and kneel before me.

270
00:18:50,580 --> 00:18:51,780
I command you.

271
00:18:53,180 --> 00:18:54,010
Never.

272
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:57,080
Sliver, now!

273
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:04,160
All right, call off your dealbound
and I shall call off my Egyptian god.

274
00:19:05,580 --> 00:19:07,640
No, you can play at this game.

275
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:10,340
Just look behind you.

276
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:16,120
Well, this is quite an
interesting predicament, isn't it?

277
00:19:17,920 --> 00:19:19,700
What to do now?

278
00:19:20,180 --> 00:19:23,960
It looks like a draw, but
looks can be deceiving.

279
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:26,820
Diabam, destroy him!

280
00:19:30,600 --> 00:19:31,780
Hold on!

281
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:33,740
That's Seto's creature!

282
00:19:35,980 --> 00:19:38,480
Sparrow, we shall save thee!
